  "network_scope": "Independent game host and guest processes on the same PC, using the active Radmin adapter address. Free Roam uses a public code, Domination uses a private invitation, DOTGOO uses UDP discovery. No second computer/tunnel is certified.",
  "verified_behavior": [
    "Four real room menu callbacks for all modes; no-room feedback; public/private invitation codec validation",
    "Host-authoritative combat and match simulation; guest entity choice and opposing-team assignment",
    "Guest physical melee kill and dash; shared Free Roam terrain and buildings; client sees moving DOTGOO creeps",
    "Host and guest Esc menus leave world/match clocks running; guest combat remains possible while host menu is open",
    "Competitive host quits to a background room with bot replacement; guest remains connected; guest quit also refills its slot",
    "Competitive menu switches to match results if the battle ends while it is open",
    "Solo Free Roam persistence and pause behavior; six-route creep-wave and solid nexus collision regressions"
  ],
  "provenance": "The three connected pairs ran against RadminMultiplayerBuildRelease. The final match-end menu cleanup was then rebuilt and verified with CompetitiveMenuEnd, ConsolidationFlow and MatchHUDCoordinates.",
